\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The energy is the undirected edge sum}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The operator #{H_0} is nonpositive.
\citet{Definition 2.1}{kigami1996kokyuroku} takes the energy
to be #{-(u,Hu)}, and \ref{fdip-00EH} identifies that
quantity with the undirected [edge sum](fdip-00EG).
The sum is not halved. The Gaussian action is a further
factor of one half and is not this energy. The conductance
#{\bigl(\frac{5}{3}\bigr)^n} is the reciprocal of the edge
resistance #{\bigl(\frac{3}{5}\bigr)^n}.}
